    {
      "name": "Wind Step",
      "category": "passive",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": null,
      "traits": [
        "air",
        "arcane",
        "transmutation"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "Haibram draws air around him to aid his movement. He Strides up to his Speed, gaining the effects of air walk and ignoring terrain while moving. He can increase the number of actions to 3 to Stride up to three times his Speed instead. Haibram begins to fall immediately after using Wind Step but treats the fall as 60 feet shorter thanks to the supporting winds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Wind Touch",
      "category": "action",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": {
        "unit": "action",
        "number": 1,
        "symbol": "◆"
      },
      "traits": [
        "air",
        "arcane",
        "evocation"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "Haibram imbues a weapon he's holding with the power of the wind until the start of his next turn. The wind's power allows Haibram to swing and hurl the weapon with great force, causing the weapon to deal an additional 2d10 damage. If the weapon does not have the thrown trait, it also gains the thrown <10 feet> trait during this attack."
      ]
    }
